# Build context for the backend image.
#
# backend/main and backend/server are compiled binaries that are committed in
# the work tree (~56 MB). They must not enter the build context, and the
# Dockerfile only builds ./cmd/server so they are never linked either.
#
# These must stay anchored to the root. An unanchored "server" would also match
# the cmd/server *directory*, which is the package being compiled.
# Same for "tmp", which is where air writes.
/main
/server
/tmp

# Local configuration and a developer-absolute REPOS_PATH.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# NOTE: docs/ must NOT be excluded. cmd/server/main.go imports it for
# `_ "backend/docs"`, which registers the generated Swagger definitions served
# at /swagger/. Removing it makes the Go build fail on a missing package.

*.log
.DS_Store
.vscode
.idea
